# Cloudflare Pages — SPA fallback
#
# Required because the site uses real paths (/products, /contact, ...)
# rather than hash URLs. Cloudflare Pages serves static files and 404s
# anything it cannot match, so without this rule a hard refresh or a
# directly opened deep link 404s -- only / would work.
#
# Static assets are matched and served before this rule, so /favicon.ico,
# /manifest.json, /sitemap.xml and /assets/* keep their real content
# instead of falling through to index.html.
#
# NOTE for a future move to Cloudflare Workers:
# Workers does NOT use this file for the SPA fallback. Configure it in
# wrangler.jsonc instead:
#
#     "assets": {
#       "directory": "./dist",
#       "not_found_handling": "single-page-application"
#     }
#
# If Worker code is added alongside the assets, you also need
# "binding": "ASSETS" and an env.ASSETS.fetch(request) fallback in the
# Worker for unmatched paths.

/*    /index.html   200
